    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12072" root="دبل" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَبُولٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دِبْلٌ</span>. Hence the saying, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَبَلَتْهُ الدَّبُولُ</span>:
see 1, near the end of the paragraph: (TA:) or
this saying is from what here follows. (K, TA.) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  A woman <i>bereft of her child by death.</i> (K.)

